@startuml fig3_data_view
' Diagram 3 of the ISO/IEC 22989 pattern: the data view.
'
' Conventions: shared/FIGURES.md. Flat boxes, no namespace prefixes, no clause
' numbers, orthogonal edges, nothing explanatory inside the drawing.
'
' What it shows: the third of the three views. What data is, how it is grouped,
' which kinds the standard distinguishes, and what is done to it before it is
' used.
'
' The disjointness of training, validation and evaluation data is asserted in
' the pattern, after the notes to 3.2.14 and 3.2.15. It cannot be drawn here
' without an edge between every pair, so the caption states it instead.
' Production data is not part of it, since it arises only during operation.
'
' Left out on purpose:
'  - the system, its tasks and its functions: diagram 1
'  - algorithms, models and parameters: diagram 2
'  - the qualities of clause 3.5: diagram 4
'
' Read left to right: where data comes from, what it is made of, what is done
' to it, and where it goes.

skinparam backgroundColor transparent
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam defaultFontSize 14
skinparam linetype ortho
skinparam nodesep 24
skinparam ranksep 42
skinparam padding 3
skinparam ArrowColor #1A2733
skinparam ArrowFontSize 13
skinparam ArrowFontColor #1A2733
hide empty members
hide circle
skinparam class {
  BackgroundColor #FCEFC7
  BorderColor #C9A227
  FontColor #1A2733
  FontSize 14
  BorderThickness 1
}

' ===================================================================
'  What data is, and how it is grouped
' ===================================================================

class Data {
  dataProp: isLabelled
}
class DataSet
class Sample
class Label

DataSet --> "*" Data   : isComposedOf
Data    --> "*" Sample : isComposedOf
Sample  --> "*" Label  : hasLabel

' ===================================================================
'  The kinds the standard distinguishes
' ===================================================================

class InputData
class TrainingData
class ValidationData
class EvaluationData
class ProductionData

Data <|-- InputData
Data <|-- TrainingData
Data <|-- ValidationData
Data <|-- EvaluationData
Data <|-- ProductionData

' ===================================================================
'  Where data comes from and where it goes
' ===================================================================

class Acquisition
class Storing
class DataSource
class DataSink

Data        --> "*" Acquisition : isAcquiredBy
Data        --> "*" Storing     : isStoredBy
Acquisition --> "*" DataSource  : hasDataSource
Storing     --> "*" DataSink    : hasDataSink

' ===================================================================
'  What is done to it
' ===================================================================

class DataProcessing
class DataProcess
class Annotation
class Augmentation
class Sampling
class Imputation
class Filtering
class Normalization
class Labelling

DataProcess <|-- Annotation
DataProcess <|-- Augmentation
DataProcess <|-- Sampling
DataProcess <|-- Imputation
DataProcess <|-- Filtering
DataProcess <|-- Normalization
DataProcess <|-- Labelling

Data           --> "*" DataProcess : isProcessedBy
DataProcessing --> "*" DataProcess : consistsOfStep

' Layout only: keep each fan of siblings on one row.
InputData      -[hidden]right- TrainingData
TrainingData   -[hidden]right- ValidationData
ValidationData -[hidden]right- EvaluationData
EvaluationData -[hidden]right- ProductionData

Annotation   -[hidden]right- Augmentation
Augmentation -[hidden]right- Sampling
Sampling     -[hidden]right- Imputation
Imputation   -[hidden]right- Filtering
Filtering    -[hidden]right- Normalization
Normalization -[hidden]right- Labelling

@enduml
